1
00:03:40,000 --> 00:03:46,000
When you wish upon a star, your dreams come true.

2
00:07:20,000 --> 00:07:26,000
Pinocchio is a animation, family, fantasy film directed by Hamilton Luske.

3
00:11:00,000 --> 00:11:06,000
When the gentle woodcarver Geppetto builds a marionette to be his
substitute son, a benevolent fairy brings the toy to life.

4
00:14:40,000 --> 00:14:46,000
The puppet, named Pinocchio, is not yet a human boy.

5
00:18:20,000 --> 00:18:26,000
He must earn the right to be real by proving that he
is brave, truthful, and unselfish.

6
00:22:00,000 --> 00:22:06,000
Pinocchio / Alexander (voice) (uncredited), played by Dickie Jones.

7
00:25:40,000 --> 00:25:46,000
Jiminy Cricket (voice) (uncredited), played by Cliff Edwards.

8
00:29:20,000 --> 00:29:26,000
Geppetto (voice) (uncredited), played by Christian Rub.

9
00:33:00,000 --> 00:33:06,000
The Blue Fairy (voice) (uncredited), played by Evelyn Venable.

10
00:36:40,000 --> 00:36:46,000
'Honest John' Worthington Foulfellow (voice)
(uncredited), played by Walter Catlett.

11
00:40:20,000 --> 00:40:26,000
Gideon (hiccup) (voice) (uncredited), played by Mel Blanc.

12
00:44:00,000 --> 00:44:06,000
Pinocchio is a 1940 American animated musical fantasy film loosely based on Carlo Collodi's 1883 novel
The Adventures of Pinocchio, produced by Walt Disney and released by RKO Radio Pictures.

13
00:47:40,000 --> 00:47:46,000
The production was supervised by Ben Sharpsteen and Hamilton Luske, and the film's sequences were
directed by Bill Roberts, Norman Ferguson, Jack Kinney, Wilfred Jackson and T.

14
00:51:20,000 --> 00:51:26,000
With the voices of Cliff Edwards, Dickie Jones, Christian Rub, Walter Catlett, Charles Judels, Evelyn Venable,  Frankie Darro, Mel Blanc and Clarence
Nash, the film follows a wooden puppet, Pinocchio, who is created by an old woodcarver, Geppetto, and brought to life by a blue fairy.

15
00:55:00,000 --> 00:55:06,000
Wishing to become a real boy, Pinocchio must prove himself to be "brave, truthful, and unselfish." Along his journey, Pinocchio encounters several characters representing the
temptations and consequences of wrongdoing, as a cricket named Jiminy, who takes the role of Pinocchio's conscience, attempts to guide him in matters of right and wrong.

16
00:58:40,000 --> 00:58:46,000
Pinocchio was a groundbreaking achievement in the area of effects animation, giving realistic movement to
vehicles and machinery as well as natural elements such as rain, water, lightning, smoke, and shadow.

17
01:02:20,000 --> 01:02:26,000
After premiering at the Center Theatre in New York City on February 7,
1940, Pinocchio was released in theatres on February 23, 1940.

18
01:06:00,000 --> 01:06:06,000
Although it received critical acclaim and became the first animated feature to win a competitive Academy Award — winning two for Best Music, Original Score and for Best Music, Original Song for "When You Wish Upon a
Star" (the latter that would later serve as the Walt Disney Company's signature song) — it was initially a commercial failure, mainly due to World War II cutting off the European and Asian markets.

19
01:09:40,000 --> 01:09:46,000
It eventually made a profit after its 1945 rerelease, and is considered one of the greatest
animated films ever made, with a 100% rating on the website Rotten Tomatoes.

20
01:13:20,000 --> 01:13:26,000
The film and characters are still prevalent in popular culture, featuring
at various Disney parks and other forms of entertainment.

21
01:17:00,000 --> 01:17:06,000
In 1994, Pinocchio was added to the United States National Film Registry for being deemed "culturally, historically, or aesthetically
significant."
In 2000, a live-action musical television film titled Geppetto was released with some elements from the 1940 film.

22
01:20:40,000 --> 01:20:46,000
A live-action remake of the same title directed by Robert
Zemeckis was released in 2022 on Disney+.

23
01:24:20,000 --> 01:24:26,000
The film explores themes of rescue, sea, child
abuse, based on novel or book, magic.
